Article 3 (Establishment and Operation of Integrated Polar Information System)
(1) The integrated polar information system under Article 13 (1) of the Polar Activities Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall include the following information:
1. Status of the development of infrastructure for polar research;
2. Status of research and development projects relating to polar regions;
3. Information on data and samples obtained through polar activities;
4. Geospatial information relating to polar regions;
5. Data collected through infrastructure for polar activities;
6. Information concerning science, policies, industries, and international cooperation relating to polar regions;
7. Information on foreign platforms that provide polar research data;
8. Other information necessary for polar activities.
(2) Where an institution entrusted with the establishment and operation of the integrated polar information system under Article 13 of the Act pursuant to Article 10 of the Decree requests the submission of materials under paragraph (2) of that Article, the institution shall specify the scope of the materials, the purposes of their retention and use, and the method of submission.
